=== SURVEY ===
Read .github\instructions\react-frontend.instructions.md, unit-conversion.instructions.md, and prompt-engineering.instructions.md.
Inspected AutomationBuilderPage.tsx, TriggerConfigurator.tsx, ConditionBuilder.tsx, ActionBuilder.tsx, automation step/input types, automation hooks, and preset API response types.
Found builder form state should stay grouped as triggers, conditions, and actions, while configurators should emit typed step inputs instead of local Builder* aliases or loose records.
Found API Automation*Input aliases are not suitable for discriminated object literal construction in the builder, so the allowed automations components folder needs a distributive step-input alias.
=== REASONING ===
Use a local distributive StepInput<T> helper under web\src\features\automations\components to remove id, automation_id, step_id, and step_order from UI step inputs without changing shared API files outside scope.
Normalize hydrated full automations and presets through explicit backend-kind switches so save payloads keep trigger_schedule/action_notify/action_command/action_set_setting and do not leak runtime metadata.
Keep the existing trigger, condition, and action UI concepts and shared UI controls; do not reintroduce trigger_config, notify_channels, record discriminators, raw controls, or old kind strings.
=== CHANGES ===
Added components\stepInputTypes.ts with typed AutomationTriggerStepInput, AutomationConditionStepInput, AutomationActionStepInput, and AutomationStepInput aliases.
Updated AutomationBuilderPage.tsx to store typed triggers/conditions/actions arrays and normalize hydrated/submitted steps by backend kind.
Updated TriggerConfigurator.tsx, ConditionBuilder.tsx, and ActionBuilder.tsx to emit typed step inputs directly.
Removed components\builderTypes.ts because Builder* aliases are no longer used.
